href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 11-05-2024, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T16:12:12-08:00","id":1500538,"title":"","content":"I just want to say I love this resumes on Exalted Product Status and I'm so happy the forum got back =)<br /> <br /> \u200bLong live Exalted =)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you like Alchemicals, please check out my DeviantArt Gallery!! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> - 5 Magic Materials BeamKlaves and Gyroscopic Chakrans ? OK<br /> - Autochthonia updated World Map? OK<br /> And many more! <a href=\"http://efq.deviantart.com/gallery/48131405/Alchemicals\" target=\"_blank\">http://efq.deviantart.com/gallery/48131405/Alchemicals</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2498-yukiartic","name":"Yukiartic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T05:47:57-08:00","id":1500601,"title":"","content":"Glad to see the forums return and thank you Blaque for the update, really great to see.<br /> <br /> I have a single question. Is it feasible to explain roughly how long the development process is from any of these stages? I'm not sure how wildly it might vary between products, nor how common slipage and rearranging of timetables is and whether this might be something that can't really be quantified. In particular and for my own selfish reasons, I'm crazy excited to see the abyssal stuff and would love to know what kind of release date something in first draft might have. Is that a thing that can be speculated, even if its just a &quot;Mid 2025&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T11:46:52-08:00","id":1500627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gribblethemunchkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500523-exalted-product-status?p=1500601#post1500601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a single question. Is it feasible to explain roughly how long the development process is from any of these stages? I'm not sure how wildly it might vary between products, nor how common slipage and rearranging of timetables is and whether this might be something that can't really be quantified. In particular and for my own selfish reasons, I'm crazy excited to see the abyssal stuff and would love to know what kind of release date something in first draft might have. Is that a thing that can be speculated, even if its just a &quot;Mid 2025&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally not, due to said variance between products. Once something hits Proofing, then it's probably going to be 1-2 months before release, the variance being because Paradox's approvals can be anything from a week to a month.<br /> <br /> However, Rich's indicated in a <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/whats-new-after-22-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">Monday Meeting</a> that the Abyssals Kickstarter is on the schedule for 2023 - it's not unfounded, as Sidereals practically zipped through the writing/editing stages, so... fingers crossed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T21:56:35-08:00","id":1500700,"title":"","content":"As excited as I am for Abyssals, Essence, and Crucible the book I'm most anticipating is the one showing by far the least movement. The last time Across the Eight Directions made an appearance in an MMN was November of 2021 and multiple books announced after it have caught up or passed it in the pipeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T05:38:37-08:00","id":1500722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500523-exalted-product-status?p=1500700#post1500700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As excited as I am for Abyssals, Essence, and Crucible the book I'm most anticipating is the one showing by far the least movement. The last time Across the Eight Directions made an appearance in an MMN was November of 2021 and multiple books announced after it have caught up or passed it in the pipeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the hold up for Across the Eight Directions is art. Particularly, map art. I could, of course, be wrong but, what I hear from artists, and friends of artists that I hang close to, is that map drawing is not fun and can be really hard.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that approval from Paradox needs to be sought for this stuff, and that can take from a couple of weeks turn around, to literal months.<br /> <br /> That said, I too am looking forward to Essence, Crucible, and Across. Abyssals never really resonated with me (mostly because they were the goth edgelords, and I never had a goth edgelord period of my life that would resonate with them), though I am highly interested in what 3e will do with them (I have been rally happy with what the other splats have done, after all, so high hope).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27754-chandramagic","name":"ChandraMagic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T09:47:57-08:00","id":1500734,"title":"","content":"The last update was Post Editing Development and Awaiting Art Notes, so it's past manuscript approval at least. Very possibly mis-remembering, but pretty sure final approval from Paradox comes in during proofing which At8D hasn't reached yet. Something to really bake your noodle, 3E KS to publish is now shorter than announcement to today for At8D. I'd pay full advance PDF price if it'd even just get me a manuscript in a heartbeat. There's so much new Creation and so many awesome sounding places that only get a sentence or paragraph in everything out so far.<br /> <br /> As for Abyssals, I definitely had my goth edgelord phase back in the day, though that's only part of why I dig 'em. Stylish undead have just kinda been my thing for a probably unhealthy portion of my life. (Pretty sure Warhammer Armies: Undead is ground zero) That said, 3E has taken my least favorite Exalt (Lunars) and second least favorite (Sidereals) and blown my mind with them and the brief teasers of Abyssals we've had are spectacular (Bleeding Lily is *chef's kiss*)\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T12:53:44-08:00","id":1500762,"title":"","content":"I haven't been on the forums in a good while and this question may have been answered elsewhere and I just haven't found it yet. Is there any word on an Infernals book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T13:17:31-08:00","id":1500764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500523-exalted-product-status?p=1500762#post1500762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't been on the forums in a good while and this question may have been answered elsewhere and I just haven't found it yet. Is there any word on an Infernals book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless they throw a hell of a curveball Infernals should be the splat following Abyssals, though as far as I know theres no official details beyond what interesting tidbits are in Essence.<br /> <br /> Would I love an insane curveball of Alchemicals first? Of course, but I'm certainly not holding my breath. \ud83d\ude02","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T23:48:30-08:00","id":1500817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500523-exalted-product-status?p=1500764#post1500764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless they throw a hell of a curveball Infernals should be the splat following Abyssals, though as far as I know theres no official details beyond what interesting tidbits are in Essence.<br /> <br /> Would I love an insane curveball of Alchemicals first? Of course, but I'm certainly not holding my breath. \ud83d\ude02</div> </div> </div> </div>Infernals should be the next fatsplat. We have no idea where they'll slot Liminals and Getimians (which won't be fatsplats but closer to the rest of the line in size).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T23:55:54-08:00","id":1500818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500523-exalted-product-status?p=1500817#post1500817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Infernals should be the next fatsplat. We have no idea where they'll slot Liminals and Getimians (which won't be fatsplats but closer to the rest of the line in size).</div> </div> </div> </div>The original stated plan (or thing roughly approximating a plan) was that Getimians and Liminals were supposed to be less-fatsplats and release in conjunction with their &quot;opponent&quot; in a vein similar to What Fire has Wrought and The Realm. Where that all stands these day is a secret known only to the gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T05:25:47-08:00","id":1500834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500523-exalted-product-status?p=1500734#post1500734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last update was Post Editing Development and Awaiting Art Notes, so it's past manuscript approval at least. Very possibly mis-remembering, but pretty sure final approval from Paradox comes in during proofing which At8D hasn't reached yet. Something to really bake your noodle, 3E KS to publish is now shorter than announcement to today for At8D. I'd pay full advance PDF price if it'd even just get me a manuscript in a heartbeat. There's so much new Creation and so many awesome sounding places that only get a sentence or paragraph in everything out so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean by approval is that I am assuming that Paradox will want to approve the maps and such, as that is, I would imagine, specifically copyrighted to Paradox. So I may be wrong about that part, either way, yes, At8D seems to be stuck in post-development hell<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Abyssals, I definitely had my goth edgelord phase back in the day, though that's only part of why I dig 'em. Stylish undead have just kinda been my thing for a probably unhealthy portion of my life. (Pretty sure Warhammer Armies: Undead is ground zero) That said, 3E has taken my least favorite Exalt (Lunars) and second least favorite (Sidereals) and blown my mind with them and the brief teasers of Abyssals we've had are spectacular (Bleeding Lily is *chef's kiss*)\u200b </div> </div> </div>Oh, agreed there. They have done amazing things with Dragonblooded (I didn't used to really care about them, because 2e didn't really care about them), Lunars (I was meh about them. All that potential, wasted in going nowhere, but 3e changed that, yay), and Sidereals (I always wanted to like them, and I did, but they were always so...oof, about many things. The manuscript shows they did wonderful things with a lot of the stuff I had issues with. The Usurpation, the factions, the Sidereals being the reason heavenly bureaucracy was breaking down; all fixed. And they even added a fucking steam train into Yu-Shan. WE CAN HAVE TRAIN CAPERS IN HEAVEN NOW). It is sad that the corebook has the problems it has though. Crucible can't come soon enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27754-chandramagic","name":"ChandraMagic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T18:55:51-08:00","id":1501203,"title":"","content":"Quick update. Abyssals and Essence Novella <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/node/2\" >Onyx Path</a> both moved-up. Aside too, currently <i>Exalted Essence</i> is having a target of layout done this week. And Exigents looks to b eone of the next books that are going to be focused on for arts.<br /> <br /> See the OP to view the complete up-to-date list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T06:43:35-08:00","id":1501400,"title":"","content":"Guess I lied, I do have more than one question.<br /> <br /> Are any of the planned books likely to give us a thorough look at demenses, manses, hearthstones and geomancy? I vaguely recall there was a book planned to look at this back when 3e launched but haven't seen anything about it since.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T11:44:25-08:00","id":1501418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gribblethemunchkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500523-exalted-product-status?p=1501400#post1501400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess I lied, I do have more than one question.<br /> <br /> Are any of the planned books likely to give us a thorough look at demenses, manses, hearthstones and geomancy? I vaguely recall there was a book planned to look at this back when 3e launched but haven't seen anything about it since.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing on the schedule.<br /> <br /> The book in question was Towers of the Mighty, which eventually got pitched under Vance and co, but nothing's been mentioned of it yet (which is not to say nothing will come of it - it took a while for Sidereals to be greenlit).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T23:58:06-08:00","id":1501781,"title":"","content":"The adventure trilogy for Essence moved to Redlines. Exalted Essence is now in Proofing, which is the last step before the final PDF gets sent out and can take a few weeks. Art moving forward steadily on <i>Crucible of Legends</i> and <i>Across the Eight Directions</i> according ot the Monday Meeting 